    "title": "Charlie Ward announces date for FAMU men's basketball home opener vs Kennesaw State - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gerald Thomas III ,\n7 hours ago Florida A&M men’s basketball’s 2025 schedule is “99 percent done,” says head coach Charlie Ward .\nAt Wednesday, Sept. 17’s 220 Quarterback Club luncheon , the newly hired Rattlers coach announced that his first home game at the Al Lawson Center will be against the Kennesaw State Owls for a non-conference matchup on Saturday, Nov. 8.\nFAMU will have two preseason exhibition games versus Edward Waters at Lawson on Tuesday, Oct. 21, and Florida State at the Donald L. Tucker Civic Center on Sunday, Oct. 26.\nFAMU at FSU will be the first time the teams have met since Saturday, Dec. 7, 1991, when it ended in a bench-clearing brawl between Tallahassee’s NCAA Division I basketball teams, leading to 18 ejections . FAMU forfeited the game after not having enough players to continue playing.\nWard was a sophomore on that FSU basketball team. He was a star quarterback for the Seminoles football team, winning the Heisman trophy and national championship in 1993 before having an 11-year career in the National Basketball Association, primarily with the New York Knicks .\nFAMU men's basketball games for 2025 season thus far FAMU men’s basketball opens its 2025 schedule on the road versus the South Florida Bulls in Tampa on Tuesday, Nov. 4, at the Yuengling Center.\nThe Rattlers will play at Central Florida on Tuesday, Nov. 11, Georgia on Monday, Nov. 17, and have a home-and-home series versus Jacksonville on the road on Tuesday, Dec. 2, and at Lawson on Wednesday, Dec. 17.\nTo start December, Ward’s Rattlers are participating in the HBCU Hoops Invitational at the ESPN Wide World of Sports Complex at Lake Buena Vista’s Walt Disney World Resort from Thursday, Dec. 4 to Sunday, Dec. 7. Barber-Scotia, Florida Memorial, and Tuskegee will accompany FAMU in the four-team tournament.\nTowards the end of the calendar year, FAMU is on the road to face Tarleton State (Dec. 19), Texas Christian (Dec. 21), and Georgia Tech (Dec. 29).\nFAMU opens Southwestern Athletic Conference play in January.\nFAMU basketball's motto under Charlie Ward: 'Chosen.' Ward was hired as FAMU’s 16th head men’s basketball coach this April, replacing Patrick Crarey II , now Grambling State’s head coach.\nHe said the mantra for his first season at the helm is ‘Chosen.’\n“We’ve all chosen to be where we are,” Ward said. “So why not go ahead and make the best of it?”\nWard has assembled a staff, which includes former Maclay head boys’ basketball coach Eugene Granger , who will be an assistant for the Rattlers.\nFAMU also has a new-look roster through many transfer portal additions, such as Jaquan Sanders , the 2022 Mr. Basketball for New York. The 6-foot-4 guard transferred from Hofstra.\n“We want to elevate the program,” Ward said. “We’re a work in progress, like most teams that have quite a few people that are coming from different places. Our goal is to learn one another.”\nReturning FAMU players Jordan Chatman and Lenard Taylor Jr., both guards, have cemented themselves as leaders for the Rattlers.\n“We have a legit chance to win every game. That’s all you can ask for going into a game as a coach ― at least you know you have a chance,” Ward said.\n“Whether you win the game or not, that’s something else. But we feel good about the team that we’ve assembled to be able to win every game. We have a chance going in.”\nGerald Thomas, III is a multi-time award-winning journalist for his coverage of the Florida A&M Rattlers at the Tallahassee Democrat.\nFollow his award-winning coverage on RattlerNews.com and contact him via email at GDThomas@Tallahassee.com or on the app formerly known as Twitter @3peatgee .\nThis article originally appeared on Tallahassee Democrat: Charlie Ward announces date for FAMU men's basketball home opener vs Kennesaw State\n3",
